WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.620
[Music]

00:00:05.630 --> 00:00:09.309
[Narrator:] Far out in the South Pacific,
a thousand miles North of New Zealand,

00:00:09.309 --> 00:00:13.209
the long swells burst on the reefs of Tonga.

00:00:13.209 --> 00:00:15.570
Once a port of call for wandering Yankee whalers,

00:00:15.570 --> 00:00:19.180
this island group lies apart from regular
trade routes.

00:00:19.180 --> 00:00:22.020
So for centuries, its people have been relatively
isolated

00:00:22.020 --> 00:00:27.489
with only occasional visitors and a small
trade in copra and bananas.

00:00:27.489 --> 00:00:30.149
But times are changing in Tonga.

00:00:30.149 --> 00:00:33.449
New markets for copra and bananas have opened
in Asia.

00:00:33.449 --> 00:00:41.360
[Music]

00:00:41.360 --> 00:00:46.820
There is a Tongan Merchant Marine with modern vessels built in Europe.

00:00:46.830 --> 00:00:50.350
The planes will bring more and more tourists
to the friendly islands.

00:00:50.350 --> 00:00:55.150
More and more islanders will leave to study
in other countries.

00:00:55.150 --> 00:00:59.450
Under the leadership of Her Majesty Queen
Salote and Prince Tungi, the Prime Minister,

00:00:59.450 --> 00:01:02.000
Tonga's relative isolation is disappearing.

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:05.689
The native government has been at once prudent
and progressive.

00:01:05.689 --> 00:01:07.540
Its benevolent rule has brought prosperity

00:01:07.540 --> 00:01:11.780
without destroying traditional customs.

00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:16.120
Looking forward to the expansion of trade,

00:01:16.130 --> 00:01:17.850
the government carefully considered the effect

00:01:17.850 --> 00:01:20.920
of increased contact with the outside world.

00:01:20.920 --> 00:01:27.479
It was realized that there was a very definite
and growing threat to the Tongan people.

00:01:27.479 --> 00:01:31.150
The population was totally unprotected against
smallpox,

00:01:31.150 --> 00:01:35.840
and smallpox is a disease which is rampant
throughout Southeast Asia.

00:01:35.840 --> 00:01:43.060
This was Tonga's problem, to vaccinate a highly vulnerable population of 70,000 against smallpox;

00:01:43.080 --> 00:01:49.240
to do it effectively, to do it immediately,
to do it inexpensively.

00:01:50.200 --> 00:02:31.540
[Music and singing.]

00:02:35.460 --> 00:02:38.920
[Narrator:] Our party came to Tonga in March of 1964

00:02:38.920 --> 00:02:41.659
in response to a request by the Tongan government.

00:02:41.659 --> 00:02:47.540
There were five of us from the U.S: four physicians
and an equipment specialist.

00:02:47.540 --> 00:02:51.459
We were going to evaluate a new, rapid, and
inexpensive means

00:02:51.459 --> 00:02:54.719
of giving smallpox vaccinations.

00:02:54.719 --> 00:02:57.809
Working together with a team of Tongan medical personnel,

00:02:57.809 --> 00:03:04.159
we would begin immediately in Nuku'alofa,
the capital city, population 20,000.

00:03:04.159 --> 00:03:09.549
We planned to immunize everyone in Nuku'alofa
within a few days.

00:03:09.549 --> 00:03:12.709
The instrument that would make it possible: the jet injector gun.

00:03:12.709 --> 00:03:16.189
This device can deliver injections as fast
as you can pull the trigger.

00:03:16.189 --> 00:03:18.909
The gun is simple to operate, and you're sure of getting

00:03:19.000 --> 00:03:21.279
the proper amount of vaccine under the skin.

00:03:21.279 --> 00:03:23.409
The gun is operated by a foot pedal;

00:03:23.409 --> 00:03:26.840
you press the pedal and then pull the trigger.

00:03:26.840 --> 00:03:32.089
This model is equipped with a new feature:
an intradermal nozzle for giving injections

00:03:32.089 --> 00:03:37.999
into the superficial layers of the skin, as
you must with smallpox vaccine.

00:03:37.999 --> 00:03:39.409
The gun is completely portable.

00:03:39.409 --> 00:03:44.109
The whole package weighs 12 pounds.

00:03:44.109 --> 00:03:46.469
Knowing that something would have to be done

00:03:46.500 --> 00:03:49.380
to get the populace interested in the immunization trial,

00:03:49.389 --> 00:03:52.329
we had prepared some informational material:

00:03:52.329 --> 00:03:58.489
films and posters telling about the dangers
of smallpox and the importance of vaccination.

00:03:58.489 --> 00:04:03.129
We delayed most of the actual planning until
after we arrived.

00:04:03.129 --> 00:04:05.400
Our Tongan associates worked with us closely.

00:04:05.400 --> 00:04:07.309
They were very eager to help,

00:04:07.309 --> 00:04:11.999
and we could not have gotten far without their
excellent advice and assistance.

00:04:11.999 --> 00:04:14.269
From the very beginning, and throughout our stay,

00:04:14.269 --> 00:04:19.589
we were given a courteous and friendly reception.

00:04:21.100 --> 00:04:24.400
The first evening we were the guests of Prince
Tungi.

00:04:24.400 --> 00:04:27.740
The Prince had personally flown to Atlanta,
Georgia in February of 1964

00:04:27.740 --> 00:04:32.530
to discuss the problem of immunizing his people
against smallpox.

00:04:32.530 --> 00:04:33.910
At the Communicable Disease Center,

00:04:33.910 --> 00:04:37.090
he met with Public Health Service officers
of the smallpox unit.

00:04:37.090 --> 00:04:40.130
It was a propitious meeting, for the unit
had just completed its study

00:04:40.130 --> 00:04:43.460
of intradermal vaccination with the new gun
developed by the Army.

00:04:43.460 --> 00:04:47.780
And the most suitable place in the world for
an evaluation of this new method was Tonga,

00:04:47.780 --> 00:04:51.250
a progressive country with a small, intact
population

00:04:51.250 --> 00:04:54.690
and no history of smallpox.

00:04:54.690 --> 00:04:56.200
During the Prince's visit to the Center,

00:04:56.200 --> 00:04:59.130
we had photographed him getting his smallpox
vaccination.

00:04:59.130 --> 00:05:02.100
This film was to be shown everywhere we went
to encourage those who would be reluctant.

00:05:05.520 --> 00:05:08.400
The people enjoyed it immensely.

00:05:08.400 --> 00:05:11.350
The next morning the vaccination drive began.

00:05:11.350 --> 00:05:14.820
The posters with our message were put up in
Nuku'alofa:

00:05:14.820 --> 00:05:21.070
Smallpox is a dread disease. Vaccination prevents
smallpox.

00:05:21.070 --> 00:05:24.090
Every effort was made to inform the people
about the vaccinations

00:05:24.090 --> 00:05:29.050
and where they could go to get them.

00:05:30.660 --> 00:05:33.500
It did not take long for them to understand
that this was being done

00:05:33.500 --> 00:05:36.560
for their protection and they cooperated wholeheartedly.

00:05:38.720 --> 00:05:40.440
One of the things we immediately realized

00:05:40.440 --> 00:05:43.280
was the importance of getting local people
to help.

00:05:43.290 --> 00:05:45.300
The teacher knows her pupils.

00:05:45.300 --> 00:05:49.970
She's the best one to reassure them, to keep
track of them.

00:05:49.970 --> 00:05:56.930
This laboratory technician checks the children
for skin rashes or lesions.

00:05:56.930 --> 00:06:01.840
We taught them our methods and they performed
many of the vaccinations themselves.

00:06:01.840 --> 00:06:07.020
The Tongans took care of the administrative
work. Their cooperation was invaluable.

00:06:07.020 --> 00:06:10.670
We were accomplishing a lot more than just
an immunization drive.

00:06:10.670 --> 00:06:18.970
We were sharing medical and public health
knowledge and experience.

00:06:18.970 --> 00:06:39.020
[Music]

00:06:39.030 --> 00:06:40.140
The children were curious,

00:06:40.140 --> 00:06:45.170
not altogether eager for the vaccination, but
well-behaved.

00:06:45.170 --> 00:06:47.800
They were expecting something unpleasant.

00:06:47.800 --> 00:06:51.500
One look at the gun and they were sure it
was going to be unpleasant.

00:06:51.500 --> 00:06:52.470
But the gun is painless.

00:06:52.470 --> 00:06:55.560
It just looks a little unfriendly, that's
all.

00:06:55.560 --> 00:07:00.820
We used a dose of one tenth cc of vaccine,
diluted 50 to 1 here.

00:07:00.820 --> 00:07:05.790
In some other places we used a 10 to 1 dilution
for comparison.

00:07:05.790 --> 00:07:07.950
Acetone was used to swab the arm.

00:07:08.740 --> 00:07:10.660
It dries faster than alcohol

00:07:10.660 --> 00:07:17.580
and prevents the intradermal head from slipping on the skin.

00:07:20.960 --> 00:07:25.140
Prince Tungi's daughter took her vaccination along with the others.

00:07:26.660 --> 00:07:34.900
Then, downtown where we took care of the government
workers, policemen, nurses.

00:07:34.940 --> 00:07:36.900
For the rest of the week we went around Nuku'alofa

00:07:36.980 --> 00:07:42.820
setting up at convenient locations, and processing thousands of people a day.

00:07:46.000 --> 00:07:48.210
After this, we went out into the countryside

00:07:48.210 --> 00:07:52.640
of the main island where we attended a once-a-year
event,

00:07:52.640 --> 00:07:55.320
the field day for all the high schools.

00:07:57.320 --> 00:08:01.740
It's quite an occasion and a major sports
attraction.

00:08:01.740 --> 00:08:07.430
When he was younger, Prince Tungi held the
pole-vaulting championship for 20 years.

00:08:07.430 --> 00:08:09.500
The Tongans are a strong, healthy people.

00:08:09.500 --> 00:08:17.280
They have no problem with heart disease, malaria,
yellow fever, or cholera.

00:08:17.300 --> 00:08:33.080
[Music]

00:08:34.840 --> 00:08:38.060
We took advantage of the field day to vaccinate
people in the crowd.

00:08:38.069 --> 00:08:43.729
We vaccinated about 1,000 people that day.

00:08:47.860 --> 00:08:50.009
At night we were busy centrifuging blood samples,

00:08:50.009 --> 00:08:53.709
going over records, and periodically disassembling
and cleaning the gun.

00:08:53.709 --> 00:08:58.790
With this remarkable instrument, a tremendous
amount of time and money was being saved.

00:08:58.790 --> 00:09:00.889
First, smallpox vaccine is expensive.

00:09:00.889 --> 00:09:03.579
With a gun you can dilute it 50 times.

00:09:03.579 --> 00:09:06.149
That's 50 shots for the price of one.

00:09:06.149 --> 00:09:08.949
Second, the conventional method of vaccination,

00:09:08.949 --> 00:09:14.730
pricking concentrated vaccine into the skin,
requires trained and experienced people.

00:09:14.730 --> 00:09:15.930
Not so with the gun.

00:09:15.930 --> 00:09:18.819
In addition, the gun virtually eliminates

00:09:18.819 --> 00:09:21.720
the sterilization problems present in the
manual method.

00:09:21.720 --> 00:09:25.050
All you have to do with the gun is to sterilize
the internal parts.

00:09:25.050 --> 00:09:29.550
It's then ready to administer thousands of
consecutive doses.

00:09:31.020 --> 00:09:34.379
After three and a half weeks on the main island, we divided up into three teams.

00:09:34.379 --> 00:09:39.009
One team remained on the main island to assess
the results of the vaccinations.

00:09:39.009 --> 00:09:42.309
The two other teams went to the northern and
central groups of islands

00:09:42.309 --> 00:09:45.749
to continue the immunization program.

00:09:45.800 --> 00:09:59.780
[Music]

00:09:59.790 --> 00:10:02.550
We went from island to island on a fish collection
boat

00:10:02.550 --> 00:10:05.870
owned by the government and used to collect
and refrigerate

00:10:05.870 --> 00:10:10.540
the scattered catches from Tongan fisherman.

00:10:10.540 --> 00:10:15.230
These boats are the only means of getting
from one place to another.

00:10:15.230 --> 00:10:19.100
We were out for three and a half weeks doing
a population of 10,000 people

00:10:19.100 --> 00:10:21.020
in the central island groups.

00:10:21.240 --> 00:10:23.480
And this was the smallest number of people,

00:10:23.480 --> 00:10:28.459
but it took us the longest time because of
the distance we had to travel.

00:10:28.459 --> 00:10:31.369
For carrying our equipment from village to
village,

00:10:31.369 --> 00:10:34.879
we used a little vehicle which was called
the ToteGote

00:10:34.879 --> 00:10:37.439
and was an attraction in itself.

00:10:37.439 --> 00:10:39.779
We went to two or three islands a day.

00:10:39.779 --> 00:10:42.230
Each evening we were the guests in a different
village.

00:10:42.230 --> 00:10:46.269
With us were a team of Tongans who were a
part of the medical department.

00:10:46.269 --> 00:10:50.540
There was a dentist, the chief medical officer,
and other personnel

00:10:50.540 --> 00:10:55.279
who utilized this trip to conduct their normal
medical calls around the island.

00:10:55.279 --> 00:10:58.249
In addition to giving protection against smallpox

00:10:58.249 --> 00:11:00.490
to the people of the outer islands,

00:11:00.490 --> 00:11:03.439
we were evaluating the effectiveness of the
diluted vaccine

00:11:03.439 --> 00:11:05.600
and the jet injector gun.

00:11:05.600 --> 00:11:09.579
To do this, we vaccinated a certain number
of people the conventional way,

00:11:09.579 --> 00:11:12.339
using the multiple pressure technique.

00:11:12.339 --> 00:11:16.420
We would later be able to compare the results
of both methods

00:11:16.420 --> 00:11:23.220
and determine the amount of protection various
dilutions of the vaccine were giving.

00:11:28.900 --> 00:11:32.380
We made two visits to each island.

00:11:32.380 --> 00:11:34.040
Once to give the injection,

00:11:34.040 --> 00:11:37.760
and the other to check the reactions two weeks later.

00:11:37.760 --> 00:11:54.059
[Music]

00:11:54.059 --> 00:11:58.639
Time after time we were paddled to and from our boat in a dugout canoe,

00:11:58.639 --> 00:12:08.239
somewhat loaded down, but with a comfortable two inches to spare.

00:12:08.240 --> 00:13:17.860
[Music]

00:13:17.860 --> 00:13:21.790
You can't truly appreciate the significance
of the work done here

00:13:21.790 --> 00:13:27.029
without considering the millions still unprotected
against smallpox.

00:13:27.029 --> 00:13:31.789
We succeeded in immunizing 80 percent of the
available population of Tonga.

00:13:31.789 --> 00:13:35.720
We did it faster, far less expensively, and
more effectively

00:13:35.730 --> 00:13:40.360
than would have been possible with standard
manual techniques.

00:13:40.360 --> 00:13:44.899
The results were read. The vaccine had taken.

00:13:44.899 --> 00:13:49.879
98.4 percent had satisfactory vaccinations,
consistently better than expected.

00:13:49.879 --> 00:13:52.290
An unparalleled success when you consider

00:13:52.290 --> 00:13:55.910
that it was carried out by such a small medical
team.

00:13:57.820 --> 00:14:01.779
Also, by observing a large population after
its first smallpox vaccination,

00:14:01.779 --> 00:14:08.179
we gained valuable scientific information
about immunity.

00:14:08.180 --> 00:14:30.280
[Music]

00:14:36.780 --> 00:14:38.840
We worked closely with the Tongan people.

00:14:38.840 --> 00:14:41.400
We shared a lot of knowledge and experience.

00:14:41.580 --> 00:14:45.480
But perhaps most important of all, Tonga and
the United States

00:14:45.489 --> 00:14:48.769
accomplished together something of great promise
to the world.

00:14:50.060 --> 00:15:03.000
For what was achieved here, on this small
Pacific island, can be extended to all people.

00:15:03.100 --> 00:15:56.269
[Music and singing.]

